    estimatedMinutes: 12,
    prompt: "Before coding you state the contract, the baseline, the chosen idea, the invariant, the complexity, and the edge cases. Here the contract is given precisely — your job is to honour every clause of it.\n\n**Contract.** Return the index of the first character in `text` that appears exactly once. If no such character exists, return `-1`. Comparison is case sensitive, and the empty string returns `-1`.\n\n**Baseline** rescans the string for each character (O(n^2)); a two-pass count is O(n).",
    exportName: "first_unique_index",
    scaffolds: { L1: "def first_unique_index(text):\n    pass", L2: "def first_unique_index(text):\n    pass", L3: "def first_unique_index(text):\n    pass", L4: "" },
