    requires: [],
    difficulty: { concept: 4, implementation: 3, recall: 3 },
    estimatedMinutes: 12,
    prompt: "Two pointers moving at different speeds locate positions you cannot index directly. When the fast pointer reaches the end, the slow pointer is halfway.\n\nReturn the value at the middle of the list, using a slow pointer that advances one step and a fast pointer that advances two. For an even length, return the **second** of the two middles. An empty list returns `None`.\n\n`[1, 2, 3]` gives `2`; `[1, 2, 3, 4]` gives `3`.\n\nA linked list is given as a plain Python list of values, in order. Return a plain Python list — the point is the pointer reasoning, not the node class.",
    exportName: "middle_value",
