    prompt: "The law of large numbers says a running average converges toward the true mean as samples accumulate. Seeing it settle is the intuition behind every claim that more data helps.\n\nReturn the running means of `samples`: entry `i` is the mean of the first `i + 1` samples.\n\n`[2, 4]` gives `[2.0, 3.0]`.",
