    estimatedMinutes: 12,
    prompt: "Self-information is `-log2(p)`: rare events are surprising. **Entropy** is the probability-weighted average of that surprise — the uncertainty in a distribution.\n\nReturn the entropy in bits of `probs`. Treat a probability of zero as contributing nothing (`0 * log 0 = 0`).\n\nA fair coin gives exactly `1.0`; a certain outcome gives `0.0`.",
    exportName: "entropy",
    scaffolds: { L1: "import math\n\ndef entropy(probs):\n    pass", L2: "import math\n\ndef entropy(probs):\n    pass", L3: "import math\n\ndef entropy(probs):\n    pass", L4: "" },
