    prompt: "Return `(cost, route)` for the cheapest path from the top-left cell of `grid` to the bottom-right, moving only right or down. `cost` is the sum of the cells entered, including both ends.\n\nRecovering the route means the full grid has to be kept, or a parallel record of which predecessor won at each cell.\n\n`route` is a list of `(row, col)` pairs starting at `(0, 0)`. Raise `ValueError` on an empty grid.",
