    prompt: "Return `(image_to_text, text_to_image, total, chance)` for a batch `similarity` matrix at a given `temperature`.\n\nDivide every similarity by the temperature, then take a softmax **along each row** and each **column**. The loss in each direction is the mean negative log probability of the diagonal cell, and `total` is their average.\n\n`chance` is the loss a random model would score, which is the natural logarithm of the batch size. Raise `ValueError` on a non-square matrix or a non-positive temperature.",
    exportName: "contrastive_loss",
    scaffolds: { L1: "import math\n\ndef contrastive_loss(similarity, temperature):\n    pass", L2: "import math\n\ndef contrastive_loss(similarity, temperature):\n    pass", L3: "import math\n\ndef contrastive_loss(similarity, temperature):\n    pass", L4: "" },
