    prompt: "Return `(by_clicks, by_rate, changed)` ranking items by raw `clicks` and by click **rate**.\n\nRaw clicks scale with how often an item was shown, so a heavily promoted item outranks better ones purely through exposure. Dividing by impressions removes that bias.\n\n`changed` is true when the two rankings differ. Break ties by item name. Raise `ValueError` when an item has more clicks than impressions, or zero impressions.",
    exportName: "exposure_corrected",
    scaffolds: { L1: "def exposure_corrected(clicks, impressions):\n    pass", L2: "def exposure_corrected(clicks, impressions):\n    pass", L3: "def exposure_corrected(clicks, impressions):\n    pass", L4: "" },
